00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.160
And...

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.040
She was the Imber's first Master.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.950
His first...?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.370
Yes. She's a former member
of Mondenkind.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.410
Her attachment to the Imber has always
been stronger than anyone else's.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.750
Those feelings probably
remain unchanged even now.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.080
Well, there's no reason they would, huh?

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.790
I'm sure neither can forget the other.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.790
Ma'am?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.120
Miss Miura, please head for Block N-5
with all due haste.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.450
Repeating, Miss Miura-

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.410
Try saying that again!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:46.330
I'm tellin' ya, the Nebula ain't movin'.
And not for a lack of adjustments.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:53.450
Don't be stupid! I've piloted it perfectly
up till now. Seven years, without a mistake!

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.700
Exactly.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:56.950
Then-

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:01.370
Which is why YOU get it too, right?
What this is about.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.000
What are you-?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.200
Please stop.
What are you-?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.500
Futami...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:10.870
Before you deployed, there was clear
disharmony between you and Nebula.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.620
You should know that, too.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.870
So why...?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:26.370
I don't think Nebula had reason
to refuse you then. But now...

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:27.700
That's not true!

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:33.540
This is a MACHINE, isn't it? If you do
the right repairs, it will move properly!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.790
I'll show you I can move it!

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:36.750
Makoto...

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.290
Please stop this!

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.580
Makoto, I'm sure you saw.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:47.830
How Haruka and the Imber looked
together. Their symphony.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.120
Shut up.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.160
Shut up!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.290
That's enough.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.290
Makoto Kikuchi, go to your quarters
and remain there.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.790
Makoto...

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.040
Did you not hear me? Go to your quarters.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:23.870
This is...

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.870
Of course, I can't say it's possible
it could've broken due to a physical shock.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:34.250
But considerin' the drop in layer index,
the Nebula's reaction, the data and so on...

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.200
The Nebula...

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.290
It rejected Makoto.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.160
You!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:48.040
Yeah, sorry. I messed up and got on the
same airplane. Wow, what a blunder.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.450
The same as that time, isn't it?

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:55.040
Ah, in any case, this thing really
got beat up, huh?

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.700
Hurts to see, doesn't it?
As the Nebula's FORMER Master.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:07.500
This really is terrible. Can it even be fixed?
The cost alone will be nothing to sneeze at.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.040
There! It was probably over there.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.000
I see.

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.790
Focus and spotting was done in a flash!

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.870
Then the killshot Nebula Punch!
It was easy!

